@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>JSONfn - Privacy</PageTitle>

<div class="page info-page">
  <div class="info-content">

    <div class="info-heading">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="info-meta">Last updated: 14 February 2026</p>
    </div>

    <p class="info-lead">
      This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>JSONfn</strong> ("we", "us", "our") handles information when you use
      <a href="https://www.jsonfn.com" class="info-link" target="_blank"
         rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.jsonfn.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">1. Data We Process</h2>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      JSONfn is a browser-based developer tool. We do not require user accounts. JSON you paste into the tool is
      processed in your browser and is not intentionally stored by us on any servers.
    </p>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      When you visit our website, the following data may be processed by us and/or our third-party advertising partner:
    </p>

    <ul class="info-list">
      <li>IP address</li>
      <li>Browser and device information</li>
      <li>Approximate geolocation inferred from IP</li>
      <li>Page visits, ad interactions, and related technical signals</li>
      <li>Cookie and similar identifier data</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">2. Advertising and Third-Party Cookies</h2>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      We use <strong>Adsterra</strong> to serve advertisements on parts of this website. Adsterra and its partners may use
      cookies and similar technologies to serve, measure, and optimize ads.
    </p>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      Adsterra publisher terms require publishers to provide a public privacy disclosure and a cookies consent message
      where cookies are placed/read for ad delivery.
    </p>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">3. Legal Basis (EU/EEA/UK)</h2>

    <ul class="info-list">
      <li><strong>Consent:</strong> advertising cookies and similar tracking technologies</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> security, core website operation, and fraud prevention</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">4. Consent, Opt-Out, and Withdrawal</h2>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      You can limit or block cookies in your browser settings at any time. Adsterra also states that disabling tools may
      be available from some third parties, but users can always disable cookies directly in browser controls.
    </p>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      For Adsterra privacy-rights requests (including California rights such as opt-out of sharing requests), see
      Adsterra's privacy contacts and rights process in their Privacy Policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">5. Third-Party Policies</h2>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      For details on how Adsterra handles data, see:
    </p>

    <ul class="info-list">
      <li>
        Adsterra Privacy Policy:
        <a href="https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy-managed/" class="info-link" target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy-managed/</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Adsterra Cookies Policy:
        <a href="https://adsterra.com/cookies/" class="info-link"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://adsterra.com/cookies/</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Adsterra Terms for Publishers:
        <a href="https://adsterra.com/publishers-terms-managed/" class="info-link" target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">https://adsterra.com/publishers-terms-managed/</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">6. Data Protection Rights</h2>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict personal data
      processing, and to object to certain processing.
    </p>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">7. Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p class="info-lead">
      We may update this policy from time to time. Changes are posted on this page with a revised date.
    </p>

    <h2 class="info-section-heading">8. Contact</h2>

    <p class="info-paragraph">
      For privacy questions about JSONfn:
      <a href="mailto:hello@jsonfn.com" class="info-link">hello@jsonfn.com</a>
    </p>

  </div>
</div>
